stream: AGENT_BROWSER_STREAM_DISABLED=1 keeps every loopback server off

Clauseo's patch to vercel-labs/agent-browser v0.41.1 (5868f7c05020e047c00e68e4abf9253cce864f41),
every OS. Upstream always starts the stream server with the daemon (port 0 only picks a random
port), and its HTTP API can drive the session. With AGENT_BROWSER_STREAM_DISABLED=1 (or true) the
daemon starts no stream server and writes no .stream file, `stream enable` fails, `inspect` and
`dashboard start` refuse to start their servers, and a daemon started with streaming on is not
reused by a CLI that has it off (the option joins the daemon's config fingerprint). This is the
part offered upstream; if upstream takes it, macOS can go back to upstream's binary. (Linux takes
upstream's binary already, for dev and CI only.)

